ven\'t seen it). Wasting it here risks losing control later when a bomb or critical moment arises.\n\n♦A is high, but again, better saved if possible. However, I must play something.\n\n♣10 is sufficient to beat ♥8 and conserves both ♦A and ♠2 for future use. It’s the minimal winning move.\n\nReason: Play the smallest card that wins — ♣10 — to beat the current trick, preserving high-value cards (especially ♠2) for critical moments later. This allows us to continue cooperating with our teammate while minimizing risk.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣10"]}'}
